course: dictionary
lesson: 997
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A boiler is a machine that heats water. You will find one in a house or building. «A boiler burns gas, or uses electricity, to heat water, and a pump sends the hot water round pipes to radiators and taps.» The clues are heat, water, pipes and radiators, so this boiler is the machine in a home.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Boiler can also mean a big closed tank where water is heated to make steam, as in an old steam engine. Look at the context to choose. If the text talks about trains, steam or history, it means the tank. If it talks about radiators, taps or pipes in a house, it means the machine.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Carbon monoxide is a poisonous gas with no colour and no smell, so homes with fuel-burning heaters or boilers need a carbon monoxide alarm.» If you put in "a machine that heats water", the sentence still makes sense. That tells you the meaning is right.
fact: A boiler is a machine that heats water for taps, baths and radiators.
fact: A boiler can also be a big closed tank where water is heated to make steam.
fact: Boilers need checking, because a broken one can leak carbon monoxide, a poison gas with no colour and no smell.
fact: «Boiler suit» is a phrase that means overalls, a one-piece work outfit.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is the right one.
exercise: «A boiler burns gas to heat water for the radiators.» What is a boiler in this sentence? | A bird that lives in the roof | *A machine in a home that heats water | A flat bed for sleeping | A type of bin for rubbish
exercise: Trains in the past had a huge boiler that made steam to push them along. What does boiler mean here? | *A big closed tank where water is heated to make steam | A machine that heats water for taps | A pump for the pipes | A pair of overalls
exercise: «Carbon monoxide is a poisonous gas with no colour and no smell, so homes with fuel-burning heaters or boilers need a carbon monoxide alarm.» Why do homes need an alarm? | Because alarms keep the boiler warm | Because boilers make a loud noise when they run | *Because a faulty boiler can leak a gas you cannot smell | Because boilers are very heavy to move
test: «A home is like a big machine with lots of parts: pipes, wires, a boiler, walls, a roof and bins that need emptying.» In this sentence, what is a boiler? | A bin for rubbish | A wire that carries electricity | *A part of a home that heats water | A type of wall
test: Which meaning of boiler fits a history lesson about old steam engines? | A machine that heats the taps in a house | A radiator on the wall | *A big closed tank where water is heated to make steam | A suit for working in
exam: «Modern condensing boilers catch heat from the steam in their fumes, which is why a white cloud comes from their pipe outside in winter.» Which meaning of boiler fits best here? | A kind of cloud | *A machine in a building that heats water | A pump that sends fumes outside | A big tank on a train only
